{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDIwL0xvc3QlMjBPbiUyMEV2ZXJlc3QlMjAlMjgyMDIwJTI5Lw","type":"movie","name":"Lost On Everest","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/nI8ZnMvlVtbXZcZN55baRDbGPn3.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/9109t2ha3nEDvhZ7n7S6QubkYHN.jpg","description":"Reaching 29,029 feet, Mount Everest has long captivated mountaineers of all stripes. But a peak that draws athletes and mountaineers to new heights isn’t without danger — or a dark side. Perhaps the peak’s greatest mystery is the missing body of Andrew “Sandy” Irvine who disappeared alongside George Leigh Mallory in 1924 just 800 vertical feet from the summit. In Lost on Everest, we follow along as a team of elite climbers with new intel on the location of his missing body set out to solve what may be mountaineering’s great mystery. Along with the body, the team hopes to find Irvine’s camera and the footage that could rewrite history.\n\nRated PG-13 · Released 15 May 2020 · United States of America · Language: English · 60 min\nStudio: National Geographic\n\nOn your server — Audio: English · Subtitle files: English","releaseInfo":"2020","genres":["Documentary","Mystery","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"7.6","runtime":"60 min","cast":["George Mallory","Andrew Irvine"],"director":["Renan Öztürk","Drew Pulley"],"released":"2020-05-15T00:00:00.000Z","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Renan Öztürk","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/8n6t81MDM1CGmdACuqDV6AtjJFV.jpg"},{"name":"George Mallory","character":"Self (Archival)","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/4hwY0Ot2DKdC2qLR1i0f5tPe2Gd.jpg"},{"name":"Andrew Irvine","character":"Self (Archival)","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/tQKyGEghB3IVTEvPCYmWlrdGXL5.jpg"}]},"country":"United States of America","language":"English","links":[{"name":"George Mallory","category":"Cast","url":"stremio:///search?search=George%20Mallory"},{"name":"Andrew Irvine","category":"